</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#(un)applicableCode -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#(un)applicableCode">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Attribute"/>
<TMF_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceApplicability</TMF_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_v1:hasStereotype>
<rdf:label>(un)applicableCode</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Indicator that specifies whether an instance represents applicability or un-applicability.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#(un)applicableDays -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#(un)applicableDays">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Attribute"/>
<TMF_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceApplicability</TMF_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_v1:hasStereotype>
<rdf:label>(un)applicableDays</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A day or days representing applicability or un-applicability.  For example 2, 3 represent Monday and Tuesday.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#(un)applicableDuring -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#(un)applicableDuring">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Attribute"/>
<TMF_v1:hasOrigin>PerformanceApplicability</TMF_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_v1:hasStereotype>
<rdf:label>(un)applicableDuring</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A period of time representing applicability or un-applicability. For example, from 8AM to 12PM.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#amount -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#amount">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Attribute"/>
<TMF_v1:hasOrigin>EmployeePay</TMF_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_v1:hasStereotype>
<rdf:label>amount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The amount corresponds to the sum of each EmployeePayComponent amount (calculated if it's a rate) for the EmployeePay period.  It specifies the unit (any currency) and the value such as $10.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#amoutPeriod -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#amoutPeriod">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Attribute"/>
<TMF_v1:hasOrigin>EmployeePay</TMF_v1:hasOrigin>
<TMF_v1:hasStereotype></TMF_v1:hasStereotype>
<rdf:label>amoutPeriod</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>amountPeriod specifies the duration covered by the amount. For example, the amount may correspond to a complete Year.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#abbreviation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#abbreviation">
