<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MarketStrategy"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_MarketStrategy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_MarketStrategy</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#OperationalMarketingPlan -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#OperationalMarketingPlan">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>OperationalMarketingPlan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An OperationalMarketingPlan defines the long-term or middle-term Marketing strategy for product placement.

The OperationalMarketingPlan is an abstract class that defines the hierarchical view of a package of OperationalMarketingPlan item.

It may be: A Composite OperationalMktPlan corresponding to several OperationalMktPlan items that are associated together within in the same marketing program. An Atomic OperationalMktPlan corresponding to a campaign plan which is the smallest level of the OperationalMarketingPlan hierarchy.

Marketing Plan is a Composite OperationalMktPlan composed of Marketing Programs

Marketing Program is a Composite OperationalMktPlan composed of Campaign Plans

A Marketing Campaign is associated to a Campaign Plan that is an AtomicOperationalMktPlan.

An OperationalMarketingPlan specifies the Budget allocated, forcasted and achieved,

         the targeted Parties (PartyProfile and PartyProfileType),

         the SaleChannel to be used,

         the ProductSpecification, ProductSpecificationType, CommercialClassification and ProductOffering it gives away or aims to place,

         the MarketingCampaignRoles involved,

         and the MarketingObjectives that must be achieved including the indicators used to evaluate the achievement (MktIndicatorSpec)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_OperationalMarketingPlan -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_OperationalMarketingPlan">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#OperationalMarketingPlan"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_OperationalMarketingPlan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_OperationalMarketingPlan</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Marketing Campaign ABE represents the strategy, or approach, for marketing new or existing ProductOfferings to identified target markets. The campaign could be for one of the following:

         The launch of a pre-paid ProductOffering with multiple promotions across SalesChannels, MarketSegments, and so forth

         A new campaign for an existing ProductOffering; the ProductOffering is not new, but the relationships, collateral, and so forth could be new

         A re-launch of a campaign for an existing ProductOffering</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Market and Sales Domain.Marketing Campaign ABE -->

