<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignWave -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignWave">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>MktCampaignWave</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>In a multichannel campaign management system, marketing campaign management requires to subdivide a campaign in several marketing campaign wave. A marketing campaign wave should use one communication mode and one target. It could be outbound or inbound.

The MktCampaignWave is the smallest operational subdivision of a campaign, with a unique target (set of segmentation criteria to define which persons or legal entities to reach), unique interaction channel (1014, 3000, external call-center), media (ads in a newspaper, ads in the subway), a duration. It may be inbound (people try to reach the CSP) or outbound (te CSP tries to reach them).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_MktCampaignWave -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_MktCampaignWave">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#MktCampaignWave"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_MktCampaignWave</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_MktCampaignWave</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WaveList -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WaveList">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WaveList</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A WaveList corresponds to the split of a MarketingCampaigns target in waves. The reason of the split might be:

         temporal splitting: wave recurrence, (ex: a non-recurrent Wave has only one Waves Recurrence);

         technical splitting (ex: limited volume in email sending, SMS sending).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

