<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ProductCategory</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ProductCategory</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProductLine -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProductLine">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ProductLine</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A method used to group related ProductSpecifications that have some characteristics in common but others that are not. For example, health monitoring device product line whose ProductSpecifications have a number of common characteristics, but come in different colors and can be used to monitor a variety of bodily functions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ProductLine -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ProductLine">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProductLine"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ProductLine</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ProductLine</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProductSpecCharacteristic -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProductSpecCharacteristic">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ProductSpecCharacteristic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A characteristic quality or distinctive feature of a ProductSpecification. The characteristic can be take on a discrete value, such as color, can take on a range of values, (for example, sensitivity of 100-240 mV), or can be derived from a formula (for example, usage time (hrs) = 30 - talk time *3). Certain characteristics, such as color, may be configured during the ordering or some other process.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

