<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_CustomerFacingServiceSpecRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_CustomerFacingServiceSpecRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Service Package ABE defines the concept of bundling a set of different CustomerFacingServiceSpecs to meet the functionality specified by one or more ProductSpecifications. This enables the shared characteristics of these CustomerFacingServices to be specified, so that multiple Products can be built from their associated ProductSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Service Package ABE defines the concept of bundling a set of different CustomerFacingServiceSpecs to meet the functionality specified by one or more ProductSpecifications. This enables the shared characteristics of these CustomerFacingServices to be specified, so that multiple Products can be built from their associated ProductSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1# hasBE_for_Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE_for_Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpec"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecAtomic"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecComposite"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Customer Facing Service Spec ABE.Service Package ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpec -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpec">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ServicePackageSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A ServicePackageSpec defines the concept of bundling a set of different CustomerFacingServiceSpecs to meet the functionality specified by one or more ProductSpecifications. This enables the shared characteristics and behavior of these CustomerFacingServices to be specified, so that multiple Products can be built from their associated ProductSpecification.
Treating this set of CustomerFacingServiceSpecs as a single object is very important for building complex Services, such as a VPN. This enables a single ProductItem (derived ultimately from a ProductSpecification) to be offered to the Customer, even though in reality the ProductItem is realized by a set of different CustomerFacingServices that must work together to provide the functionality that the Customer needs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpec -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpec">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpec"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpec</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecAtomic -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecAtomic">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ServicePackageSpecAtomic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A ServicePackageSpecAtomic object models different ServicePackageSpecs as a set of different instances of individual, independent CustomerFacingServiceSpecs. This is fundamentally different than the ServicePackageSpecComposite object, which is used to model one ServicePackageSpec as the combination of other existing ServicePackageSpecs (as well as providing its own extensions).
For example, GoldPackageSpec is an individual packaging of services, and is therefore an instance of the ServicePackageSpecAtomic class. If there was a service offering that combined the services defined by the GoldPackageSpec with those defined by another ServicePackageSpecAtomic class, such as the PlatinumPackageSpec, then that combination could be aggregated together, forming an instance of the ServicePackageSpecComposite class.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecAtomic -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecAtomic">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecAtomic"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecAtomic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecAtomic</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecComposite -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecComposite">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ServicePackageSpecComposite</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This models different packages as the combination of other existing ServicePackages (as well as providing its own extensions). This is fundamentally different than ServicePackageAtomic, which models different ServicePackages as a set of different instances.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecComposite -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecComposite">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ServicePackageSpecComposite"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecComposite</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ServicePackageSpecComposite</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Resource Facing Service Spec ABE defines the common characteristics for a set of ResourceFacingServices. This scales by enabling multiple ResourceFacingServiceSpecs to be defined to model the common characteristics of different groups of ResourceFacingServices.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Resource Facing Service Spec ABE defines the common characteristics for a set of ResourceFacingServices. This scales by enabling multiple ResourceFacingServiceSpecs to be defined to model the common characteristics of different groups of ResourceFacingServices.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1# hasBE_for_Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE_for_Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpec"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecVersion"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#RFSSpecVersionDetails"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Service Specification ABE.Resource Facing Service Spec ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpec -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpec">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceFacingServiceSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The ResourceFacingServiceSpec represents the technical solutions that the Service Provider can implement for CustomerFacingServiceSpec.
Each technical solution (ResourceFacingServiceSpec) requires ResourceSpecifications to be realized and might require buying part of the solution to a supplier (for example the Service Provider might have to buy the Local Loop to provide a broadband access).
This is the base entity for defining different types of ResourceFacingServiceSpecs. A ResourceFacingServiceSpec is an abstraction that defines the shared characteristics of a particular ResourceFacingService. The shared portion serves as a single common basis to build a set of variable ResourceFacingServices that all use this common ResourceFacingServiceSpec.
This class can be thought of as a template, which represents a generic specification for implementing a particular type of Service. A ServiceSpecification may consist of other ServiceSpecifications supplied together as a collection.  Members of the collection may be offered individually or collectively. ServiceSpecifications may also exist within groupings, such as within a Product. ServiceSpecification inherits from EntitySpecification, which inherits from RootEntity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpec -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpec">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpec"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpec</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an abstract base class for defining ResourceFacingServiceSpecifications that do not have any subordinate ResourceFacingServiceSpecifications. In other words, a ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic is a stand-alone ResourceFacingServiceSpecification, and doesnt require any supporting ResourceFacingServiceSpecifications to define the shared characteristics (i.e., attributes, relationships, and constraints) of any ResourceFacingServices that it serves as a template for.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an abstract base class that defines an integrated set of ResourceFacingServices that collectively meets the needs of a CustomerFacingService. For example, the Customer may have requested "GoldService", which is a ServicePackage that defines a set of ServiceBundles, each of which has its own QoS. Each individual ResourceFacingService that is part of the ServicePackage can be derived from a ResourceFacingServiceSpecification. In this case, a ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite will aggregate all of the individual ResourceFacingServiceSpecifications into a single named object.
This object is a stand-alone object. However, it consists of other ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite and/or ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic entities. That is the primary difference between this entity and the ResourceFacingServiceSpecAtomic entity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_ResourceFacingServiceSpecComposite -->

