<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ConfigurationFeature -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ConfigurationFeature">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ConfigurationFeature</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A ConfigurationFeature is a type of Entity described by a ConfigurationFeatureSpec.

It is used to expose one or several ResourceFunctions to a consumer in such a way that it is easier to configure these RFunctions from a consumer view point.

A ConfigurationFeature may have characteristics configured according to the possible configurations specified by the ConfigurationFeatureSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

