<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Chip -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Chip">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>Chip</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a concrete class that models different types of chips that are either directly configurable by the end-user (e.g., a programmable device) and/or represent FRUs (e.g., a special ASIC that can be upgraded by replacing it with a new version of that same ASIC).

Note that capacity characteristics (e.g., how much memory can a Flash chip hold) are defined through the PhysicalCapacity association.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

