<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PhysicalResourceRole"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Physical Resource ABE.Physical Role ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Physical Resource ABE.Physical Role ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PhysicalResourceRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PhysicalResourceRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>PhysicalResourceRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is representing the different types of roles that various physical resources can take on. Two specialized roles have been defined: holder and adapter. This enables a single object, such as a Card, to have additional functions. For example, a Card may also serve as a motherboard or hosting board for another Card. In this situation, there isnt a separate EquipmentHolder - rather, the Card acts as a holder in addition to providing its normal functions.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

