<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#EmployeePay -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#EmployeePay">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>EmployeePay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>EmployeePay describes pay information for an Employee such as salary, bonus or any other monetary benefits.

This is useful reading all changes over a period of time. This is further defined with the frequency amount pay group. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_EmployeePay -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_EmployeePay">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#EmployeePay"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#/amount"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#/amoutPeriod"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_EmployeePay</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_EmployeePay</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#EmployeePayComponent -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#EmployeePayComponent">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>EmployeePayComponent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>EmployeePayComponent is where an Employees components of pay is defined. Each section of their pay is defined as an individual line item and can have different frequencies or currencies.

This entity includes effective dated history.  Pay Component object stores all elements that are paid to employees like: base salary bonus target car allowance. 

For each pay component you need to define  
 If the component is recurring or a one time payment 
 If recurring the frequency 
 If it is paid as an absolute amount or percentage 
 If percentage what is it a percentage of (other Pay Component or Pay Component Group 
 If it is an earning or a deduction 
 If it is actual pay or target 
 If it is taxable or non-taxable 
 If it should be visible in Self Service 
 If it is used by compensation planning  Recurring pay components such as base salary should be defined with recurring attribute set to Yes and target attribute set to No. </rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_EmployeePayComponent -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_EmployeePayComponent">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#EmployeePayComponent"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#amount"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_EmployeePayComponent</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_EmployeePayComponent</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PayComponentSpecification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PayComponentSpecification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>PayComponentSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>PayComponentSpecification specifies components of a pay that might correspond to fixed salary, bonus...

Some of them have fixed amount and other amount might not be pre-defined when it can be specific to an employee while respecting PayRange threshold (minimum and maximum pay).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_PayComponentSpecification -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_PayComponentSpecification">
