<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationCost"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationType"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationVersion"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecRelationship"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Work Specification ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Work Specification ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecFulfillmentRate -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecFulfillmentRate">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecFulfillmentRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Entity that is used in Planning and WorkSpecification configuration. Represents a rate that shows how many particular work tasks (quantity attribute) can be performed by a given organization in a given location (or serving areas) with a given capacity (Consumption Capacity attribute). For example, with 100 man hours of Fiber layout skills, 200 works of Dig a trench for Underground Cable, 200m length can be performed in an urban area by an organization.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecFulfillmentRate -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecFulfillmentRate">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecFulfillmentRate"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#consumptionCapacity"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#quantity"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#standardDrivingTime"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecFulfillmentRate</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecFulfillmentRate</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>WorkSpecification describes the characteristics of a type of (manual) work. The characteristic/characteristic value pattern may be applied for WorkSpecification (and work as an instance). For example, WorkSpecification could be Assembly of server blade in a shelf.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecification -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecification">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecification"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isAppointmentRequired"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#standardCapacityRequired"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#standardDuration"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecification</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationCost -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationCost">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecificationCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A monetary amount assigned to a WorkSpecification that represents the cost to the business to plan, develop, and implement the WorkSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationCost -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationCost">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationCost"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#costToBusiness"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationCost</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationCost</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecificationRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an abstract base class that defines a WorkSpecification in terms of a set of roles which are then used to characterize the invariant functionality of the Work. For example, a specification of cable layout work can have the role of network build, or the role of a service fulfillment task.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationRole -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationRole">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationType -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationType">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecificationType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A classification that groups WorkSpecifications that share common characteristics. For example, Equipment maintenance work type, or network trouble shooting type. This class can be used to present a Catalog of work specifications.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationType -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationType">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationType"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationType</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationVersion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationVersion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecificationVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A particular form or variety of a WorkSpecification that is different from others or from the original. The form represents differences in properties that characterize a WorkSpecification that are not enough to justify the creation of a new WorkSpecification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationVersion -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationVersion">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecificationVersion"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#date"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#number"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationVersion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecificationVersion</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecRelationship -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecRelationship">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSpecRelationship</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This association class specifies the relationship between WorkSpecifications. For example, an equipment maintenance work task requires a service re-routing work task. Note: this Relationship will affect the Relationship between corresponding WorkItems, i.e. WorkOrderFulfillment (start-to-start, start-to-finish, etc.) in Project ABE, as well as the Scheduling mechanism.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecRelationship -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecRelationship">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSpecRelationship"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecRelationship</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSpecRelationship</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>WorkforceResource ABE represents the employees and other non-human resources involved in field operations.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>WorkforceResource ABE represents the employees and other non-human resources involved in field operations.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1# hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePool"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceOrganizationRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforcePoolAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePool"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceTool"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Resource ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePool -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePool">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceEmployeePool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an employee pool, as a set or group of employees available for assignment to work tasks. A WorkforceOrganizationRole can have many workforce pools, and vice versa, a pool can contain employees from more than one organization. Examples of a Pool are Fiber installation team, service repair team, etc. A Pool contains people/resources with particular skills, availability, location, other restrictions, and preferences. Pool is associated with Capacity. For example, a WorkForceEmpolyeePool shows that on July 1, from 8 am to 12 pm there are 100 man hours available with the skill of fiber layout for the New York area. A detailed model of the capacity of the pool down to timeslot, skill/work level is a subject for a future SID release.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePool -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePool">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePool"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isWfSupplierEmployeePool"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePool</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an association class and defines specific characteristics for the assignment of an employee to a pool. For example, assignment of fiber technicians to the Installation and Repair team pools, serving the New York Area in the first quarter.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#poolAssignmentRestriction"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeePoolAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceEmployeeRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a PartyRole that represents individuals who are involved in the workforce process as employees with particular skills. For example, Field Technician, Network Engineer, Supervisor, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeRole -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeRole">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#skillLevel"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceOrganizationRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceOrganizationRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceOrganizationRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is a PartyRole that represents organizations involved in field operations. It can be the CSP Field Technician department itself, or a 3rd-party contractor company. Note that OrganizationRole has Calendar, inherited from Calendar of PartyRole.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceOrganizationRole -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceOrganizationRole">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceOrganizationRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#organizationRoleName"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceOrganizationRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceOrganizationRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforcePoolAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforcePoolAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforcePoolAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An abstract class representing assignment of an employee or other resource to a pool. An employee can be assigned to more than one pool. The attribute poolAssignmentRestriction is a place holder that represents any limitation of the assignment other than time period. Pool assignment will update available capacity WorkSchedule of some organization.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforcePoolAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforcePoolAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforcePoolAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#poolAssignmentRestriction"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforcePoolAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforcePoolAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePool -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePool">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceResourcePool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents a resource pool as a set of resources (both physical and logical) available for assignment to work tasks. For example, the Dallas pool for fiber rollout for a weekday contains X number of trucks, Y number of test kits, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePool -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePool">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePool"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isWfSupplierResourcePool"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePool</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an association class and defines specific characteristics for the assignment of a resource to a pool. For example, assign a fiber test kit to the Dallas Pool for July.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#poolAssignmentRestriction"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourcePoolAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceResourceRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Defines the concept of various types of roles associated with WorkforceResources (both physical and logical). For example, tools (meter, ladder), Truck, GPS, Handheld, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceRole -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceRole">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleCombination"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleSelectionMethod"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceTool -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceTool">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceResourceTool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An example class that represents the specific role of workforce resources. Examples are tester kits, GPS, Trucks, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceTool -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceTool">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceTool"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleCombination"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#roleSelectionMethod"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceTool</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceTool</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1# hasBE_for_Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE_for_Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Work"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkRole"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Workforce Resource ABE.Work ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Work -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Work">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>Work</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Work entity is used to record actual executed work, i.e. an instance of that entity is created for the actual work described by the WorkSpecification. If there are characteristics defined for the WorkSpecification, the work instance has a distinct value assigned for those characteristics. Instances of Work are associated to the WorkOrderItem. The quantity attribute can be used if the same work has been done more than once identically (based on the similar attribute in WorkOrderItem).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Work -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Work">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Work"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#quantity"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_Work</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_Work</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkRole -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkRole">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>This is an abstract base class that defines a Work task in terms of a set of roles which are then used to characterize the functionality of the Work. For example, a particular work of fiber rollout at a location at a certain date can play the role of a build task of an infrastructure project or the role of an installation task in a service fulfillment project.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkRole -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkRole">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkRole"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkRole</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkRole</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Workforce Schedule ABE defines reservation and assignment of a technician or resource to a task.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Workforce Schedule ABE defines reservation and assignment of a technician or resource to a task.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1# hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeReservation"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceReservation"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSchedule"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Workforce ABE.Workforce Schedule ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceEmployeeAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an assignment of a particular WorforceEmployeeRole for a particular work task in a specific timeframe. For example, assignment of a person in a network engineer role to a trouble shooting work task for at least 2 hours. The assignment is associated with a CalendarEntry of an Assignment WorkSchedule.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeReservation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeReservation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceEmployeeReservation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an implementation of a request for reservation of work time in some human resource pool. It is also possible to reserve the work time of an individual employee. Note: the reservation, or booking according to appointment, is associated to Calendar Entry. The CalendarEntry here can belong to a reservation WorkSchedule. This Calendar entry may be floating. Once the Reservation becomes an Assignment (to be dispatched), a particular time slot (Calendar Entry) can be fixed in the WorkSchedule.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeReservation -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeReservation">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceEmployeeReservation"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeReservation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceEmployeeReservation</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceResourceAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an assignment of a particular resource for particular work in a specific timeframe. For example, assignment of a fiber test kit (or, additional example, a role of a test kit) to a fiber rollout work for a date.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#actualCost"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceReservation -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceReservation">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkforceResourceReservation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Represents an implementation of a request for the reservation of usage time in some resource pool (tools, trucks, materials, etc.). It is also possible to reserve usage time of a particular resource.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceReservation -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceReservation">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkforceResourceReservation"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceReservation</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkforceResourceReservation</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSchedule -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSchedule">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>WorkSchedule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Being a subclass of SimpleCalendar, WorkSchedule and its variants describes various appointment, reservation, and assignment schedules of an organization. For example, a WorkSchedule shows that a contractor team responsible for the New York area has been receiving 100 requests for fiber installation during July and is currently scheduled to perform 80 of them.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSchedule -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_WorkSchedule">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#WorkSchedule"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#granularity"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#calendricalSystem"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_WorkSchedule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_WorkSchedule</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain.Enterprise Risk ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain.Enterprise Risk ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>Represents all items that relate to risk of an enterprise. It also concerns security vulnerabilities and related events as well as information related to Revenue Assurance such as areas of revenues leakage risk and operational capability to resolve any detected degradations and violations.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Enterprise Domain.Enterprise Risk ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Risk ABE.Revenue Assurance ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Risk ABE.Revenue Assurance ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Revenue Assurance area of the SID provides revenue assurance controls, revenue assurance violations, revenue assurance key performance indicators (KPIs), revenue assurance objectives, and rules that map revenue assurance KPIs and threshold violations to revenue assurance trouble tickets.  Additionally, the scope of Revenue Assurance includes revenue assurance actions/responses that reconcile revenue assurance trouble tickets and bring the trouble tickets to closure.

Revenue Assurance ABE Level 2 Executive Summary

Revenue leakage is considered a cost of doing business in the telecom industry. Revenues are lost due to several reasons such as network provisioning, mediation and CDR errors, billing and interconnect inconsistencies, lost of data and corrupted files, fragmented support systems and manual or fuzzy business processes.  Revenue Assurance research reports estimations are that the degree of exposure varies in the range of the 3% to 15% percent of the carriers revenue depending on factors such as services type, geography, carrier type, and RA maturity level.

The main question for any business is how much leakage is acceptable and how to improve the operations and systems in such a way that minimizes those leakages.  Effective Revenue Assurance (RA) process must ensure the data integrity and synchronization across all the disparate systems and the network itself, in order to ensure operational and financial efficiency.  Such process provides analysis of the relationship between network resources, services, customers, and generated revenue, and will enable the service provider to detect revenue leakage (e.g. un-billed customers, mis-billed customers), stranded assets, and operational inefficiencies.

In addition, a process management layer is required to allow RA managers and Financial Directors to enjoy the benefits of their achievements, track the revenue leakage identification, quantification and reclamation processes and easily report the results. A big challenge for RA and communications business in general is to move gradually the focus of process management away from resolving and reacting to problems that repeatedly occur, and towards the prevention of problems before they occur.

The Revenue Assurance area of the SID provides revenue assurance controls, revenue assurance violations, revenue assurance key performance indicators (KPIs), revenue assurance objectives, and rules that map revenue assurance KPIs and threshold violations to revenue assurance trouble tickets.  Additionally, the scope of Revenue Assurance includes revenue assurance actions/responses that reconcile revenue assurance trouble tickets and bring the trouble tickets to closure.

The Revenue Assurance ABE is a sub-ABE from Enterprise Risk ABE located in the Enterprise Domain.

The Revenue Assurance Control ABE defines policy-based rules that represent the logical definition of comparisons performed on entities, such as bills and call detail records (CDRs), to identify Revenue Assurance Violations.  The Revenue Assurance Violation ABE models discrepancies identified based on applying the rules defined by Revenue Assurance Control entities.  

Revenue Assurance KPI ABE models KPIs and Revenue Assurance Objectives whose violation trigger Revenue Assurance Trouble Tickets.  KPIs are defined on Revenue Assurance Violations and on other revenue assurance related entities, such as bills and CDRs.  Revenue Assurance Trouble Ticket ABE entities represent trouble tickets opened to resolve one or several causes (for example, Revenue Assurance Violations) that resulted in a Revenue Assurance KPI not meeting a Revenue Assurance Objective.

Revenue Assurance Action/Response ABE entities represent the result of reconciling Revenue Assurance Trouble Tickets by initiating and performing a series of one or more activities. Revenue Assurance Action/Response ABE entities also model the root cause for Revenue Assurance Trouble Tickets based on rules that trigger root cause analysis.

Revenue Assurance Assessment ABE entities measure the effectiveness of Revenue Assurance Controls, Revenue Assurance Objectives, and Revenue Assurance KPIs. Revenue Assurance Assessment ABE entities include recommendations of refining controls, objectives, and KPIs.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Enterprise Risk ABE.Revenue Assurance ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

