<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Patch"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_Patch</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_Patch</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerability -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerability">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecurityVulnerability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>An information security "vulnerability" is a mistake in software that can be directly used by a hacker to gain access to a system or network. 

CVE considers a mistake a vulnerability if it allows an attacker to use it to violate a reasonable security policy for that system (this excludes excluding entirely "open" security policies in which all users are trusted, or where there is no consideration of risk to the system). 

For CVE, a vulnerability is a state in a computing system (or set of systems) that either: 

   - allows an attacker to execute commands as another user 

   - allows an attacker to access data that is contrary to the specified access restrictions for that data 

   - allows an attacker to pose as another entity 

   - allows an attacker to conduct a denial of service 

source:  http://cve.mitre.org</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerability -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerability">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerability"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#cceName"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#cveName"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#disclosureDateTime"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#discoveredDateTime"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#exploitPublishedDateTime"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#lastModifiedDateTime"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#publishedDateTime"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#reference"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#technicalDescription"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerability</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>It is the instance of a particular SecurityVulnerability that has been classified into one of the three categories (software flaw, software feature misuse, or software configuration issue). 

Notes: For example (hypothetically), Internet Explorer could have a bug that is categorized as a software flaw.   There can be vulnerabilities that have one or more of the three category types associated with it.  In this case, the vulnerability would be scored for all three types.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryType -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryType">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Identifies the type of SecurityVulnerability for the purposes of vulnerability scoring.



Notes: The three types defined include software flaws, security configuration issues, and software feature misuses.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryType -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecurityVulnerabilityCategoryType">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
