<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Security Vulnerability ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Security Vulnerability ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of SecurityVulnerabilityMetricDefn that does not have any subordinate SecurityVulnerabilityMetricDefns, that is, an AtomicSecurityVulnerabilityMetricDefn is a leaf-level SecurityVulnerabilityMetric.  

Notes: Examples include Base Metrics - Access Vector, Authentication, and Access Complexity.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#datatype"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#scoringSequence"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_AtomicSecVulScoringMetricDefn</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of SecurityVulnerabilityMetricDefn that is formed by aggregating other SecurityVulnerabilityMetricDefns, which may be Composite or Atomic SecurityVulnerabilityMetricDefns.

Notes: A Base Score Metric which is made up of Base Exploitability and Base Impact, Base Exploitability made up of Acess Vector, Authentication, and so forth.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#datatype"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#scoringSequence"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_CompositeSecVulScoringMetricDefn</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A standard value for a defined scoring metric (SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn).  Each metric has multiple instances which represent multiple values.

Notes: For example,  Base Metric Access Vector has three pre-defined values - L/Local, A/Adjacent Network, and N/Network.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefn</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The definition of a metric which may be categorized into three groups (Base, Temporal, and Environmental).  These three groups are further decomposed into groupings for exploitability and/or impact which define metrics used to score vulnerability severity.  

Notes: For example, Base Metrics are grouped into Base Exploitability and Base Impact Metrics.  Base Exploitability Metrics include Access Vector, Authentication, and Access Complexity Metrics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#datatype"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#scoringSequence"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefn</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The scoring system specification defines three groups of metrics to determine a score a vulnerability. 

Notes: The three types of metrics include Base Metrics, Temporal Metrics, and Environmental Metrics.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringMetricDefnAssignment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A standardized method for vulnerability measurement and severity scoring.

Notes: Three scoring specifications have been created, one for each of the categories of system vulnerabilities defined by NIST SCAP.  They include the Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS)  which address software flaw vulnerabilies (introduced in 2004/v2 in 2007), the Common Misuse Scoring System (CMSS) which was designed for measuring and scoring misuse vulnerabilities.  And the Common Configuration Scoring System (CCSS) which addresses software security configuration issue vulnerabilities.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#version"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoringSystem</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment></rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE"/>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1# hasBE_for_Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE_for_Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasBE"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoreAlgorithm"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoreAlgorithmMember"/>
<rdfs:comment>hasBE_for_Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>hasBE_for_Security Vulnerability Scoring Definition ABE.Security Vulnerability Scoring Algorithm ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of SecVulnerabilityScoringAlgorithmMember that indicates some combination of delimiter, operator, value should be used at this point in the algorithm.  The combination is dependent on the value(s) present for the three attributes that describe this entity.

Notes:  For example,  "20 *"  , "*", "/".</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#delimiter"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#operator"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#value"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#sequence"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityGeneralMbr</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of SecVulnerabilityScoringAlgorithmMember that indicates the score of the associated SecurityVulnerabilityMetric should be used at this point in the algorithm.

Notes:  For example, the score for the Access Vector should be used at this point in the algorithm Exploitability score = 20 *  Access Vector score * Authentification score * Access Complexity score.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#sequence"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricDefnMbr</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A type of SecVulnerabilityScoringAlgorithmMember that indicates the value of the associated SecurityVulnerabilityMetricValue should be used at this point in the algorithm.

Notes:  For example, Access Vector = case of Access Vector value of L:  .395, where L is the value of the Acess Vectors security vulnerability metric value; A:  .646; N:  1.0.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#sequence"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityMetricValueDefnMbr</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoreAlgorithm -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SecVulnerabilityScoreAlgorithm">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SecVulnerabilityScoreAlgorithm</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A step-by-step procedure for calculating the a security vulnerability score.

Notes: For example, BaseScore = round-to-1-decimal(((0.6 * Impact) + (0.4 * Exploitability) - 1.5) * f(Impact)).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SecVulnerabilityScoreAlgorithm -->

