<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#achievedBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#allocatedBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#forecastBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unit"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_AtomicBudget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_AtomicBudget</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Budget -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Budget">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>Budget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A Budget contains the different budgets allocated to at least one Party. The Party might be an Organization. A Budget might be split into several parts related to a sub-division of the initial Budget.

A Budget specifies the unit used for each amount: allocated, forecasted and achieved.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Budget -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Budget">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Budget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#achievedBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#allocatedBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#forecastBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unit"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_Budget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_Budget</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeBudget -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeBudget">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>CompositeBudget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CompositeBudget is a type of Budget.

A CompositeBudget is broken down into Budgets atomic or not.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CompositeBudget -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CompositeBudget">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#achievedBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#allocatedBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#forecastBudget"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#unit"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_CompositeBudget</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_CompositeBudget</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#FinancialAccount -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#FinancialAccount">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>FinancialAccount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A FinancialAccount is part of the sub-ledger accounting that aggregates the amounts of one or more party accounts owned by a given party. Its an internal view of the CSP to manage incomes and outcomes. It is only an internal accounting which does not need to follow the GeneralLedger accounting regulation.

Each accounting event from a PartyAccount is logged to a FinancialAccount according to the assignment rules specified by PartyAccountAssignment.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_FinancialAccount -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_FinancialAccount">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#FinancialAccount"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_FinancialAccount</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_FinancialAccount</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Common Domain -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Common Domain">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>The Common domain represents business roles, information and activities (e.g. business entities, business processes, functions, logical applications, interfaces, metrics, etc.) that support other Frameworx domains and are not specific to (i.e. are generic) or owned by any particular domain, or are referenced or utilized from two or more other domains.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Common Domain</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Common Domain.Anomaly ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Common Domain.Anomaly ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>Anomaly ABE represents any unusual or unexpected event, observation, pattern, or item that is significantly different from the norm that an enterprise wishes to detect, analyze, assess and mitigate within an autonomous environment.  In order for the autonomous operations environment to behave within the calibrated operational level, anomalies may require administrative and operational guidance.  Anomaly ABE entities provide a means of defining boundary conditions and lifecycle behavior for Anomalies, as well as providing control over the end-to-end management process for Anomalies.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Common Domain.Anomaly ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Common Domain.Anomaly ABE -->

