</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SegmentSpecification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SegmentSpecification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SegmentSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A Segmentation might be decomposed as Segments each of them being a combination of Conditions (combined with AND or OR). These Segments are specified thanks to the SegmentSpecification.
Segmentation might be defined so that segments might be disjoined or not, continuous or discontinuous.
For example, the market segmentation of Orange contains several segmentations Pan European, Sub-Saharan Africa, each of  them being decomposed as combined conditions (Ex: Pan European Segmentation decomposed as Mobile reluctant, Basic Communicators, Pragmaticssegments).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SegmentSpecification -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SegmentSpecification">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SegmentSpecification"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#lowerSize"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#triggeringEvent"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#upperSize"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SegmentSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SegmentSpecification</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SegmentationSpecification -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SegmentationSpecification">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>SegmentationSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A SegmentationSpecification specifies rules (CriterionCondition) to divide a large set of Entitys instances into subsets according to criteria. These subsets are called segments.
For example, Market segmentation divides a broad target market into subsets of consumers, businesses, or countries that have, or are perceived to have, common needs, interests, and priorities, and then designing and implementing strategies to target them.
We mainly consider Parties segmentation, but we could also segment other concepts such as InstalledResources, Projects
For example, we could define rules to identify InstalledResources that have a high level of risk of failure.
The SegmentationSpec is evaluated to produce the corresponding Segmentation according to a triggering event. It might be one shot, a periodicity or at any update of criteria.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SegmentationSpecification -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_SegmentationSpecification">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#SegmentationSpecification"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#triggeringEvent"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_SegmentationSpecification</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_SegmentationSpecification</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CriterionCalculationRule -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CriterionCalculationRule">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>CriterionCalculationRule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CriterionCalculationRule is a type of PolicyRule used to specify how to calculate the value of a Criterion.
The rule is evaluated when an event occurs. If the condition clause is satisfied, then the pass-action clause will be executed; otherwise, the fail-action clause will be executed.
In a CriterionCalculationRule, the action corresponds to the Criterions calculation and if needed the record of it.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CriterionCalculationRule -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CriterionCalculationRule">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CriterionCalculationRule"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasSubRules"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isCNF"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#isMandatoryEvaluation"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#usage"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#keywords"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#policyName"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_CriterionCalculationRule</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_CriterionCalculationRule</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Criterion -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Criterion">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>Criterion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Criterion is the definition of information classifying an Entity from the model (represented by an instance of RootEntityType).
A Criterion classifies only one RootEntityType, i.e. it helps grouping instances of only one Entity of the Orange SID model.
Examples:
         the Criterion Age classifies a Party (instance Party of RootEntityType)
         the Criterion Installation city classifies an InstalledResource
A Criterion might be
         either existing information related to an Entity
              in this case we need to specify where the information can be found 
                 the Attribute carrying the Criterion information (RootEntityTypeCharSpec)
                 the Entity carrying the Criterions Attribute
                 and the Relationship between the Entity classified by the Criterion and the Entity where the Criterion can be found (RelationshipType)
         or information that has to be calculated
              in this case we need a rule that specifies when it has to be calculated and how to calculate the information (cf. CriterionCalculationRule)
              the calculated information might be recorded or not. 
                 If not, it is only used to evaluate the condition for the Criterion. 
                 If yes, we need to specify where it has to be recorded
                      the Attribute carrying the Criterion information
                      the Entity carrying the Criterion Attribute
                      and the Relationship between the Entity concerned by the Criterion and the Entity where the Criterion is recorded
Note: 
         Only attributes carried by an Entity directly related to the Entity concerned by the Criterion can be specified to record the Criterions value.
         As many relationships might exist between the Entity classified and the Entity carrying the Criterion attribute, we may need to specify which type of relationship is concerned (RelationshipType)</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Criterion -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Criterion">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Criterion"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_Criterion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_Criterion</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CriterionCondition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>CriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A CriterionCondition specifies a condition expressed using Criteria.
A CriterionCondition might be Atomic or Composite.
Each AtomicCriterionCondition specifies a condition on a Criterion such as If Age = 36.
Each CompositeCriterionCondition combines two or more AtomicCriterionConditions specifying if all the AtomicCriterionConditions must be True (AND) or if at least one of them must be True (OR).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CriterionCondition -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CriterionCondition"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_CriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_CriterionCondition</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeCriterionCondition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeCriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>CompositeCriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Each CompositeCriterionCondition combines two or more AtomicCriterionConditions specifying if all the AtomicCriterionConditions must be True (AND) or if at least one of them must be True (OR).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CompositeCriterionCondition -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_CompositeCriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#CompositeCriterionCondition"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#compositionType"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_CompositeCriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_CompositeCriterionCondition</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicCriterionCondition -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicCriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>AtomicCriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Each AtomicCriterionCondition specifies a condition on a Criterion such as If Age = 36.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_AtomicCriterionCondition -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_AtomicCriterionCondition">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#AtomicCriterionCondition"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_AtomicCriterionCondition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_AtomicCriterionCondition</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Segment -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Segment">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>Segment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>A Segment is the result of applying a SegmentSpecification when a triggeringEvent occurs.
The validity period is calculated according to the triggering event.
The Segment classifies RootEntitys instances for which the CriterionCondition is True when it is built.
The attribute respectsThreshold specifies if the Segment respects the lower and upper size defined by the SegmentSpecification.
A Segment might be composite. A CompositeSegment corresponds to the sum of the composed Segments.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Segment -->

<owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_Segment">
<rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute"/>
<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Segment"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#respectsThreshold"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_Segment</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_Segment</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#TMFDomain"/>
<rdfs:comment>A Digital Identity ABE contains all Business Entities used for enabling identification / authentification of Party or Resource in order to allow Party or Resource to use their permission carried by their roles.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Business Entity.Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ABE"/>
<rdfs:comment>A Digital Identity ABE contains all Business Entities used for enabling identification / authentification of Party or Resource in order to allow Party or Resource to use their permission carried by their roles.</rdfs:comment>
<rdfs:label>Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasDomain_for_Common Domain.Digital Identity ABE -->

