<rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementSpec"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#expectedDuration"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#type"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_ProjectElementSpec</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_ProjectElementSpec</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementRelationship -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ProjectElementRelationship">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>ProjectElementRelationship</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>-         The ProjectElementRelationship allows relating ProjectElements. A ProjectElement might be linked to several ProjectElements.
Ex: a ProjectElement not being able to start until another ProjectElement has been completed.
The ProjectElements can be related by two types of relationships: Dependency or Replacement.
A Dependency is where the two Project Elements have some starting or finishing dependency. E.g. Activity 2 cannot start until Activity 1 is complete.
A Replacement is where one or more ProjectElements are replaced by one or more other ProjectElements.
Each type of relationship might be subdivided into several kinds: 
The subtypes of Dependency are:
before-start-delay: Activity2 starts at least lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
before-finish-delay: Activity2 starts at least lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
after-start-delay: Activity2 finishes at least lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
after-finish-delay: Activity2 finishes at least lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
start-equal-start: Activity2 starts exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
start-equal-finish: Activity2 starts exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
finish-equal-start: Activity2 finishes exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 starts
finish-equal-finish : Activity2 finishes exactly lag timepoints after Activity1 finishes
The subtypes of Replacement are:
Substitution: This is a one for one replacement. E.g. Activity 1 is no longer valid and has been replaced by Activity 1A
Division: This is a one for many replacement. E.g. Activity 1 is no longer valid and has been replaced by Activities 1A, 1B and 1C
Fusion: This is a many for one replacement. E.g. Activities 1A, 1B and 1C are no longer valid and have been replaced by Activity 1Z</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

