<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#status"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#validFor"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#description"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#ID"/>
<rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#name"/>
<rdf:label>hasAttribute_for_PolicyEventSpecComposite</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>hasAttribute_for_PolicyEventSpecComposite</rdfs:comment>
</owl:ObjectProperty>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PolicyEventSpecType -->

<owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#PolicyEventSpecType">
<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#BE"/>
<rdf:label>PolicyEventSpecType</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The PolicyEventSpecType class defines a generic category of PolicyEventSpecs. Each PolicyEventSpecType serves to group a set of particular PolicyEventSpecs that share the same behavior and other semantics. One result of this is to be able to more efficiently define a set of related PolicyEventSpecs that can be grouped together to form a higher-level, or composite, PolicyEventSpec.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:Class>

<!--http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#hasAttribute_for_PolicyEventSpecType -->

