<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Market and Sales Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Assurance"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage Sales Problem business activity is in charge directing and controlling the handling of issues and pinpoints that affects selling products and services.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.1.21.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Sales Problem</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Manage Sales Problem business activity is in charge directing and controlling the handling of issues and pinpoints that affects selling products and services. 

Manage Sales Problem includes tasks that mange handling of failure in sales strategy, unreliable Sales Pipeline Management, poor sales performance and effectiveness, a lack of sales team focus, misalignment with marketing, and/or poor product/service sales experience.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Sales Problem -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Sales Problem">
