<rdf:label>Associate Product Offering with Product Offering Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Associate Product Offering with Product Offering Catalog associates a product offering and applicable product offering prices with a catalog. The product offering may have been developed by an enterprise or on-boarded from another party.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Exchange Product Offering Catalog -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Exchange Product Offering Catalog">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Exchange a product offering catalog with another party.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.3.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Exchange Product Offering Catalog</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Exchange Product Offering Catalog exchanges a catalog with another party engaged in the value fabric. The exchange may be sending a product offering catalog to another party or receiving one from another party.

It uses the generalized Exchange Catalog process to exchange a catalog, in this case a product offering catalog.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Offering Agreement Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Offering Agreement Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Develop a template agreement that defines the terms/conditions associated with a product offering.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Agreement Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Agreement Management develops a template agreement that defines the terms/conditions associated with a product offering. The terms/conditions are accepted by a party when the offering is acquired.

This process uses the general Party Agreement Management process to develop a template agreement. It's focus is on defining product offering terms/conditions, such as financial terms (which includes such things as acceptable methods of payment), shipment terms, and service term (which includes early termination fees). It also associates an offering and price(s) with the terms/conditions and with a template agreement.

Note that Party Agreement Management is also used to define template service level agreements and associate them to a product offering and/or a product specification.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define terms/conditions for a product offering agreement.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.4.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Product Offering Agreement Terms/Conditions defines product offering terms/conditions, such as financial terms (which includes such things as acceptable methods of payment), shipment terms, and service term (which includes early termination fees). 

The terms/conditions are accepted by a party when the offering is acquired.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Associate Product Offering and Price with Product Offering Agreement -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Associate Product Offering and Price with Product Offering Agreement">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Associate a product offering and price(s) with a product offering template agreement and the product offering and price(s) with the terms/conditions.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.4.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Associate Product Offering and Price with Product Offering Agreement</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Offering Prototyping -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Offering Prototyping">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Iteratively develop a product offering to a state that enables it to be tested in some way.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Prototyping</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Prototyping iteratively develops a product offering. Product Offering Development andamp; Retirement processes develop each iteration of the offering to a state that enables it to be tested in some way by the Product Offering Development andamp; Retirements Conduct Product Offering Acceptance Testing process. Tests can be conducted internally, in the form of a pilot, or field trial. Tests are measured against defined acceptance criteria. Identified improvements/enhancements are made during the next iteration based on test results. Once the final iteration tests are accepted the offering is rolled out and launched to the market at large.

Note: This process is not further decomposed, because the process uses existing Product Offering Development andamp; Retirement processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Offering Promotion Development -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Product Offering Promotion Development">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Develop a promotion for one or more product offerings delivered using different mediums (television, radio, print, online) that advertise the promotion to reach the market, customers and channels.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.6</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Product Offering Promotion Development</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Product Offering Promotion Development develops a promotion for one or more product offerings delivered using different mediums (television, radio, print, online) that advertise the promotion to reach the market, customers and channels.

Product offering promotions can be designed with different ends in mind, including introducing a new product, retaining customers, bringing in new customers, and increasing sales of a product already on the market.

Product Offering Promotion Development works with other processes, such as Market Research, Marketing Campaign Management, Marketing Communications, and Advertising Management to design the promotion and advertising. One of the key roles of all these processes is to position the product in the market, especially versus competitive products.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Product Offering Promotion Scope -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Product Offering Promotion Scope">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define the specific product promotion scope to be used for positioning the product offering(s) involved in the promotion in the marketplace.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.6.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Product Offering Promotion Scope</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Ensure Product Offering Promotion Capability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Ensure Product Offering Promotion Capability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Not used for this process element.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.6.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Ensure Product Offering Promotion Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Ensure that there is capability (for example, information, materials, systems and resources) so that the product promotion can begin and managed. Monitor planned promotions and redistribute existing capability or enable new capability (people, facilities, infrastructure).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Develop Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Develop Product Offering Promotion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage all activities and stakeholder engagement to develop and agree on a product offering promotion and the selection of appropriate channel or channels to support delivery of the promotion.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.6.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Develop Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Develop Product Offering Promotion manages all activities and stakeholder engagement to develop and agree on a product offering promotion and the selection of appropriate channel or channels to support delivery of the promotion. It also interacts with Marketing Communications to develop promotional messages and Marketing Campaign Management to associate promotions with a campaign.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Create Product Offering Promotion -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Create Product Offering Promotion">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Engage with stakeholders engagement to develop a product offering promotion and associate it with applicable marketing campaigns and marketing communications.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.6.3.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Create Product Offering Promotion</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Not used for this process element</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Product Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Business Value Development"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Select the appropriate channel or channels to support delivery of a product offering promotion.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.2.7.2.6.3.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Select Product Offering Promotion Delivery Channels selects the appropriate channel or channels to support delivery of a product offering promotion. A particular promotion may require selection of one or several delivery channels.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Obtain Product Offering Promotion Agreement -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Obtain Product Offering Promotion Agreement">
