<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Strategy and Planning -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Strategy and Planning">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Develop the strategies and policies of the enterprise for engagement with its existing and potential customers.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.17</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Customer Strategy and Planning</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Customer Strategy andamp; Planning processes develop the strategies and policies of the enterprise for engaging with its existing and potential customers. To support the enterprises market, sales and operations strategy, the Customer Strategy and Planning processes develops the policies for customer engagement, interaction and security. For example, the enterprise decides that it will outsource some of its processes for customer fulfillment and customer support for one or more of its service lines or customer segments; both the functional processes, as well as Infrastructure and Product Lifecycle Management processes. The effectuation of this is done according to policies and strategies set by the Customer Strategy and Planning processes.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Acquisition Strategy and Plan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Acquisition Strategy and Plan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define Customer Acquisition Strategy and Plan processes enable establish actions that create a systematic, and sustainable acquisition strategy for customers, and includes evolving customer acquisition based on new trends and changes.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.17.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Customer Acquisition Strategy and Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Customer Acquisition Strategy andamp; Plan processes establish the activities that manage the enterprises preferences for customers, and processes for bringing new customers or clients to the business. 
The goal of this set of processes is to create a systematic, sustainable acquisition strategy that can evolve with new trends and changes. It allows the business to: Make money to meet costs, and reinvest in growth, and show evidence of traction for outside parties such as investors, partners, and influencers.
This process was named -  Customer Acquisition Strategy andamp; Planning</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Retention Strategy and Plan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Retention Strategy and Plan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define Customer Retention Strategy and Plan processes enable develop the strategic management plan following a set of activities that keep customers the organization has invested into acquiring.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.17.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Customer Retention Strategy and Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Customer Retention Strategy andamp; Plan defines the activities that enable the organization to provide and extract more value from existing customer base.
The set of processes enable develop a strategic management plan with a set of actions that keeps customers the organization has invested into acquiring. 
The strategy and plan help deliver services that are consistent with the organization value proposition and brand. This includes developing programs to increase customer loyalty and decreasing turnover.

This process was named Customer Retention Strategy andamp; Planning</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Engagement Strategy and Plan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Engagement Strategy and Plan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define Customer Engagement Strategy and Plan processes plan the delivery of a sustained or increasing customer satisfaction by having more positive interactions with customers and the outcomes are more fitted to their needs.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.17.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Customer Engagement Strategy and Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The set of processes to plan the delivery of a sustained or increasing customer satisfaction by having more positive interactions with customers.
It can be through any channel, from in person, to online, to over the phone. Great strategies take customer engagement from reactive to proactive.

This process was named Customer Engagement Strategy andamp; Planning</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Support Strategy and Plan -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Customer Support Strategy and Plan">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Strategy Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define Customer Support Strategy and Plan processes enable establish the strategic management activities and plans that handle customer support and customer service interactions in a way that creates consistent customer experiences, while enabling the organization to examine customers perception and expectations across all journeys.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.17.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Customer Support Strategy and Plan</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Customer Support Strategy andamp; Plan processes ensures that a Customer Service Strategy is a thorough plan to handle customer interactions. It lets the organization provide a consistent customer experience throughout the customer journey.
A customer support plan establishes methods and techniques to deeply examine customers' perceptions and expectations of the organization, and guides the company through the process of bringing its customer service activities in line with customers' needs.
Improved customer experience results in a more loyal customer base. Loyal customers buy more often, spend more, and refer their friends and family to the organization either through social structures.

This process was Customer Support Strategy andamp; Planning</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Management Capability Delivery -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Management Capability Delivery">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Customer Management Capability Delivery processes create and maintain capabilities required to uphold full knowledge and control over all customer interactions as well as develop and deploy capabilities  to achieve the best customer experience.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.19</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Customer Management Capability Delivery</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of the Customer Management Capability Delivery processes is to create and maintain the required capabilities needed to: 
- effectively generate and retrieve insights from customer activities; 
- ensure the organization has the capability to meet the customer's contact and interaction expectations.
- create the total capabilities required to support the delivery of customer support in a timely, effective and reliable way to customers; 
- create capabilities to design internal views of Customer Journey templates to which particular customer engagements can be mapped and processed for multiple interactions, multiple channels, multiple intents.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Analytics Capability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Analytics Capability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Deliver Customer Analytics Capability  processes implement  the supporting processes and technology needed to effectively generate and retrieve insights from customer activities.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.19.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Deliver Customer Analytics Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deliver Customer Analytics Capability processes implement  the supporting processes and technology needed to effectively generate and retrieve insights from customer activities.
Deliver Customer Analytics Capability ensures the organization has the capabilities e.g., skills, processes and technology to effectively operationalize  analytics.
Such capabilities enable the design and implementation of structures and resources required to operationalize the  collection and analysis  of customer engagement data, and generation of customer insights needed to make predictions of customer events/activities, and generate recommendations to customers.

Was named Customer Analytics Capability Delivery</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Order Capability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Order Capability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Deliver Customer Order Capability processes ensure there are capabilities to meet customer's expectations of order interactions and management across all channels and products.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.19.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Deliver Customer Order Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deliver Customer Order Capability processes ensure there are capabilities such as processes and technology to meet customer's expectations of order interactions and management across all channels and products.
This set of processes ensure the organization implements the capability to sense and manage customer demand accurately, respond to changing delivery expectations, and to accurately  manage promised timelines based on fulfillment planning lead times and estimates. 

 Was named Deliver Customer Order Capability</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Support Capability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Support Capability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Deliver Customer Support Capability processes ensure the organization has the capabiliites required to ensure  customer support in a timely, effective and reliable way to customers.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.19.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Deliver Customer Support Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deliver Customer Support Capability processes enable planning and effective delivery of the total capabilities required to ensure customer support in a timely, effective and reliable way to meet all existing and potential customer needs for products and services offered.
This involves integration of capabilities available from within the enterprise, as well as from external parties. 
Was named Customer Support Capability Delivery</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Engagement Capability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Deliver Customer Engagement Capability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Capability Management"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Deliver Customer Engagement Capability processes ensure the organization has the capabilities required to design and use internal views of Customer Journey templates to which particular customer engagements can be mapped and processed.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.19.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Deliver Customer Engagement Capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Deliver Customer Engagement Capability processes are responsible for designing  the capabilities required to design and use internal views and Customer Journey templates to which particular customer engagements can be mapped and processed.
Customer engagement has multiple interactions, multiple channels and multiple intents. The Deliver Customer Engagement Capability process creates capabilities to align specific engagement needs and also simplify Customer Journey views so that similar engagements can be unified into common process flows.
was named Customer Engagement Capability Delivery</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Privacy Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Customer Privacy Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness and Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Customer Privacy Management processes manage the privacy requirements of customers in accordance with customers' information privacy requirements, and regulatory mandates. 
This process is used to create and define the customer privacy profile type; manag</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.21</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Customer Privacy Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Customer Privacy Management processes manage the privacy requirements of customers in accordance with customers' information privacy requirements, and regulatory mandates. These processes help to: 

	Define the Customer Privacy Management scope,
	Define the information that constitutes Personally Identifiable Information (personal identifiable information) where Privacy Policy applies,
	Define Default Privacy requirements for each type of personal identifiable information,
	Capture Customers explicit consent and define with Customers a Privacy Policy according to their wishes and the processing entities default Privacy Policy possible values,
	Modify/update Privacy Policy according to future needs or requirements,
	Enforce the Customer Privacy Policy and ensure that Customer information is managed correctly according to stated privacy policies,
	Communicate relevant personal identifiable information processing standards to third parties with whom the information is shared.
</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Customer Privacy Definition -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Customer Privacy Definition">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness and Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Customer Privacy Management Definition process is used to define the privacy management that applies to the category of customer.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.21.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Privacy Definition</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The Customer Privacy Management Definition process manage the definition of the privacy management that applies to a particular category of customer.
It is used to determine the legal expectations of entities that want to apply and use customer information (such as jurisdiction, location, regulation, and standards).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Customer Privacy Profile -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Manage Customer Privacy Profile">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness and Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Customer Privacy Profile Management process is used to administer the Privacy Profile for each Customer Privacy Profile Type, including the enforcement of the Customer Privacy Profile; Processes to display, and modify the Privacy Profile, and the import/e</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.21.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Manage Customer Privacy Profile</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Customer Privacy Profile Management process is used to handle the life cycle of the customers privacy profile.
This process is crucial to customer privacy management, because it helps the entities processing data to conform with Laws andamp; Regulation and privacy by design principles. It is composed of:

	Enforcement of the Customer Privacy Profile, meaning the application of the Privacy Rules for each purpose/retention, both internal and external, of a Customers personal identifiable information.
	Import/export of the Privacy Profile for each element of personal identifiable information received or sent from or to another entity involved in the processing of customer data.
	Modify a Privacy Profile, through Dashboards or consent.
	Meet other requirements from regional Laws andamp; Regulations, such as the demonstration of compliance, the Right of Erasure or Right to be forgotten.
</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Modify Customer Privacy Policy -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Modify Customer Privacy Policy">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Customer Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Operations Readiness and Support"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Modify Customer Privacy Profile process is used to modify the rules of privacy profiles following an agreement of a privacy profile between the organization.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.3.21.2.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Modify Customer Privacy Policy</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Modify Customer Privacy Profile process is used to modify the rules of privacy profiles following an agreement of a privacy profile between the organization and a customer.
Such modifications may occur in the Dashboard and honored according to the requirements stipulated by a by privacy policy type.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Erase Customer Privacy Profile Information -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Erase Customer Privacy Profile Information">
