<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Mediate Business Partner Interactions -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Mediate Business Partner Interactions">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Business Partner Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG.Assurance"/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manages conversion of externally received messages into the required internal enterprise formats, and manages conversion to agreed externally send message formats.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.0.7.10.7.3</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.6.9.6.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Mediate Business Partner Interactions</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>The purpose of the Mediate Business Partner Interactions is to ensure that transaction message structure and interactions conform to agreed or externally defined or agreed standards used by the enterprise and its Parties. Increasingly transactions with external parties (e.g. Parties using RosettaNet or Web Services standards) will need to conform to message and data formats defined by third parties or third Business Partner organizations.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

