<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Knowledge Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Knowledge Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Knowledge Management business activity manage the establishment, assessment, operations and evaluation of processes and capabilities that support knowledge capture, knowledge organization, knowledge operations and knowledge evaluation across the enterpris</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.3.4.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Knowledge Management business activity manage the establishment, assessment, operations and evaluation of processes and capabilities that support knowledge capture, knowledge organization, knowledge operations and knowledge evaluation across the enterprise. Knowledge Management processes support the organization across a gamut of key activities including protecting its intellectual properties, business resilience and as well manages the standards for creating and managing information and information capture and stored, assigned, and distributed. Knowledge in the enterprise includes both the tacit and explicit knowledge contained with the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assess Knowledge Management Needs -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assess Knowledge Management Needs">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Assess Knowledge Management needs business activity analyzes to understand the knowledge needs of enterprise functions, translated the business needs into knowledge management targets and identify knowledge management activities to address the needs.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Assess Knowledge Management Needs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Knowledge Management needs business activity analyzes to understand the knowledge needs of enterprise functions, translated the business needs into knowledge management targets and identify knowledge management activities to address the needs. Assess Knowledge Management Needs ensures that assessment of the process and capabilities for knowledge management capture current state of knowledge management activities across enterprise functions. The assessment process solicits input from enterprise functions and 'Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance' to identify improvements for knowledge management.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Establish Knowledge Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Establish Knowledge Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Establish Knowledge Management business activity sets up the processes and capabilities that are required to institutionalize and operationalize knowledge management activities across all the enterprise.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Establish Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Establish Knowledge Management business activity sets up the processes and capabilities that are required to institutionalize and operationalize knowledge management activities across all the enterprise.  Establish Knowledge Management business activity leverage the strategic Initiative of the enterprise as an input to make knowledge management support the business goals. It includes defining 'knowledge management lifecycle' and 'implementing knowledge management capabilities'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Knowledge Management lifecycle -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Knowledge Management lifecycle">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Define Knowledge Management Lifecycle business activity is responsible for describing all the stages that support knowledge management across the enterprise.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.2.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Define Knowledge Management lifecycle</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Define Knowledge Management Lifecycle business activity is responsible for describing all the stages that support knowledge management across the enterprise. Define Knowledge Management Lifecycle defines 'who', 'what', 'when', 'where' and 'how' of activities that support institutionalizing and operationalizing knowledge management. This includes description of expectation for the creation, sharing, auditing, organizing and storage of knowledge in support of the enterprises business goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Implement Knowledge Management capability -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Implement Knowledge Management capability">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Implement Knowledge Management Capability business activity puts into effect the required capabilities (processes, people and technology) that support operationalizing knowledge management activities.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.2.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Implement Knowledge Management capability</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Implement Knowledge Management Capability business activity puts into effect the required capabilities (processes, people and technology) that support operationalizing knowledge management activities.  Implement Knowledge Management Capability covers the processes and mechanisms that support the acquisition to dissemination of  knowledge within the enterprises business functions, and with stakeholders.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Operate Knowledge Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Operate Knowledge Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Operate Knowledge Management business activity controls and administers day-to-day tasks that support knowledge acquisition, knowledge organization, knowledge refinement, knowledge storage, knowledge distribution and knowledge application.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Operate Knowledge Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Operate Knowledge Management business activity controls and administers day-to-day tasks that support knowledge acquisition, knowledge organization, knowledge refinement, knowledge storage, knowledge distribution and knowledge application. Operate Knowledge Management supports enterprise business functions to identify knowledge objects, run different knowledge operation models, and address their knowledge handling goals.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Acquire Knowledge -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Acquire Knowledge">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Acquire Knowledge business activity handles gathering or collecting knowledge from various sources, including discovering knowledge based on value it brings to the organization.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.3.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Acquire Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Acquire Knowledge business activity handles gathering or collecting knowledge from various sources, including discovering knowledge based on value it brings to the organization.  This business activity adds new knowledge to a knowledge base and support 'Refine Knowledge', 'Distribute Knowledge' and 'Apply Knowledge'.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Organize Knowledge -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Organize Knowledge">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Organize Knowledge business activity handles the classification, mapping, indexing, and categorization of knowledge to support activities that acquire, store and retrieve knowledge.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.3.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Organize Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Organize Knowledge business activity handles the classification, mapping, indexing, and categorization of knowledge to support activities that acquire, store and retrieve knowledge.  The enterprise needs to make  connections between different knowledge objects. With connections from knowledge objects, the enterprise structures knowledge in a way that accurately and meaningfully organizes knowledge for refinement, storage, distribution and application.  Organize Knowledge uses "systems" and processes to generate, transform, manage, use, and transfer knowledge-based products and services to achieve enterprise business goals and objectives.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Refine Knowledge -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Refine Knowledge">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Refine Knowledge business activity handles the evaluation, analysis and optimization of knowledge to be stored by the enterprise.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.3.3</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Refine Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Refine Knowledge business activity handles the evaluation, analysis and optimization of knowledge to be stored by the enterprise. Refine Knowledge enables the enterprise to iteratively improve its knowledge operations activities in an effort to improve the quality of the enterprises knowledge objects.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Store Knowledge -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Store Knowledge">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Store Knowledge business activity handles the storage of knowledge objects to support the enterprises knowledge management goals.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.3.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Store Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Store Knowledge business activity handles the storage of knowledge objects to support the enterprises knowledge management goals.  Store knowledge ensures the organization can formally account for knowledge it in its possession through well-defined storage medium/media.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Distribute Knowledge -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Distribute Knowledge">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Distribute Knowledge business activity handles tasks that assign and share knowledge among enterprise business functions through various defined techniques, people, and technologies.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.3.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Distribute Knowledge</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Distribute Knowledge business activity handles tasks that assign and share knowledge among enterprise business functions through various defined techniques, people, and technologies.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance business activity assesses performance of knowledge management outcomes based on how knowledge management lifecycle and knowledge management operations support the achievement of business goals.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.4.4</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance business activity assesses performance of knowledge management outcomes based on how knowledge management lifecycle and knowledge management operations support the achievement of business goals.  Evaluate Knowledge Management Performance supports 'assess knowledge management needs', 'establish knowledge management', and 'knowledge management operations' by preventing repeated missteps, guiding development, and sharing of knowledge to give the enterprise and its business functions a competitive edge.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Financial Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Financial Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Manage the financial management aspects of the enterprise.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>1.3.5.1</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.5</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Financial Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Financial Management processes manage the financial aspects of the enterprise such as Treasury, Banking, Payroll, Financial Planning and Accounting Operations functions, e.g., Accounts Receivable and Payable. These processes are accountable for the financial health of the enterprise, managing cash flow, etc.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Financial Management Approach -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Define Financial Management Approach">
