<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Collect Learner Feedback</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Collect Learner Feedback business activity supports 'Evaluate Learning Program' by managing activities that result in receiving information from learners about the learning program.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assess Learning Performance -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assess Learning Performance">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Assess Learning Performance business activity analyzes the  learning activities that support a learning program to evaluate levels of understanding of curriculum and content used in learning programs.  Assess Learning Performance helps to acquire learning</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.15.6.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Assess Learning Performance</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Learning Performance business activity analyzes the  learning activities that support a learning program to evaluate levels of understanding of curriculum and content used in learning programs.  Assess Learning Performance helps to acquire learning performance information from both the learning program, and individual learning plans using any or both of direct and indirect approach.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Training Management -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Training Management">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Training Management business process manage activities that instruct and deliver matters of technical knowledge according to learning management goals.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.16</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Training Management</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Training Management business process manage activities that instruct and deliver matters of technical knowledge according to learning management goals.  Training Management ensures the most effective approach and capability is available to transmit knowledge or information. Training Management is core to the organization being able to match capability and capacity to provide impactful means to the organizations knowledge management goals. The practice of Training Management includes directing and organizing all the training activities for the organization, including assessing training needs, designing the training, implementing the training (such as scheduling and timing the instruction activities, handling training logistics) and evaluating training outcomes against needs.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assess Training Needs -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Assess Training Needs">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Assess Training Needs business activity evaluates training gaps and needs, sets training objectives, evaluates roles, prepares plans and identifies place, people, process and technology capacity required to conduct and achieve a specified training objecti</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier></TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.16.1</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Assess Training Needs</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Assess Training Needs business activity evaluates training gaps and needs, sets training objectives, evaluates roles, prepares plans and identifies place, people, process and technology capacity required to conduct and achieve a specified training objective. Assess Training Needs lays the necessary groundwork for determining the enterprises  needs and how participants in the training will best receive the required training. Assess Training Needs captures skills proficiency of participants, frequency of skill usage and level of participants skill value to performance. Output of an Assess Training Need business activity include a map of participant (who) and type of training approach that will be most impactful (how, what, when).</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

<!-- http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Design Training Program -->

<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Design Training Program">
<rdf:type rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Process"/>
<TMF_v1:hasDomain rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#Business_Entity.Enterprise Domain"/>
<TMF_v1:hasVerticalGroup rdf:resource = "http://www.semanticweb.org/igork/ontologies/2024/1/TMF_v1#VG."/>
<TMF_v1:BriefDescription>Design Training Program business activity develops the blueprint of capabilities and facilities that achieve training performance goals based on the enterprises learning objectives and knowledge management goals.</TMF_v1:BriefDescription>
<TMF_v1:MaturityLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4</TMF_v1:MaturityLevel>
<TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>X.X.X.X.X</TMF_v1:OriginalProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>1.7.16.2</TMF_v1:ProcessIdentifier>
<TMF_v1:ProcessLevel rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</TMF_v1:ProcessLevel>
<rdf:label>Design Training Program</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment>Design Training Program business activity develops the blueprint of capabilities and facilities that achieve training performance goals based on the enterprises learning objectives and knowledge management goals.  Design Training Program correlates Learning Management objectives and prior Training Management lessons into training strategies most appropriate for participants. It includes designing the Training Objectives, Developing Training Plan and identifying the type/way/method to implement training (supervised: hands-on; unsupervised: simulation, experiential etc.) that is appropriate and impactful to participants.   The output of Design Training activity eradicates the gaps in training and with capability and facilities that assure better training performance.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

