<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">3786</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Product Test Restitution Design</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Product Test Restitution Design Function specifies Test rules defining the restitution of the result depending on test execution context.
For example: a test result of ok/not ok can be enough for a user whereas customer care may requires more details in the result of the test.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

