<TMF_v1:hasUID rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">2154</TMF_v1:hasUID>
<rdf:label rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">Anomaly Pattern Matching</rdf:label>
<rdfs:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString">This function compares the detected anomalies with known anomaly patterns to find similarities and differences. It will compare observed patterns to known patterns (either anomalous or non-anomalous) to identify matches. It takes input from a dataset and a set of known patterns, and output matches between the observed and known patterns.</rdfs:comment>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

